glTF files with morph / blend target data are now supported for model components in the engine. Two new shader constructs are now exposed that can be used to achieve morph target rendering:

```glsl
// 1) a uniform / constant that holds the weights
uniform vs_uniforms
{
	vec4 morph_targets_weights;

	// if you need to support more than 4 weights, use an array instead:
	// vec4 morph_targets_weights[x];
};

// 2) an array sampler that holds the morph target data
uniform sampler2DArray morph_targets;
```

Demo: 
[morph-target-testing.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26677227/morph-target-testing.zip)

Future improvements:
* Instancing - a new vertex attribute semantic is needed
* Mix skinning and morph animations - currently an animation can drive either a skinned animation or a morph target animation, not both
* Play multiple morph animations at the same time (also applies to bone animations)

